# The SQLite database is a BUILD ARTIFACT — rebuilt from data/*.csv by
# `python db/load.py`. The CSV checkpoints are the source of truth; do not
# version-control the binary DB (it would churn on every mutation and bloat
# the repo). Run `python db/load.py` after a fresh clone to rebuild it.
db/investment_tracker.db
db/investment_tracker.db-wal
db/investment_tracker.db-shm
db/investment_tracker.db.bak

# Landing-page sign-up captures — runtime data written by app/server.py
# (POST /api/leads). Not part of the reproducible CSV->SQLite pipeline; the
# operator reads this file directly. Never commit emails to the repo.
data/leads.csv

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Atomic-write temp files (db/export_csv.py + calculate_scores.py write to
# *.tmp then os.replace; a stray .tmp means a write was interrupted)
*.tmp

# Test-run SQLite sidecars (tests build/clean tests/_tmp_update.db;
# the -wal/-shm sidecars can leak and should not be committed)
tests/_tmp_update.db-wal
tests/_tmp_update.db-shm

# Session scheduler lock (runtime artifact, not source)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# PRIVATE / internal documents — not published in the public repo.
# Kept locally only. (History was rewritten to purge prior copies.)
InvestmentExecutionDatabase-goal.md
docs/project-roadmap.md
docs/project-monetization.md
docs/superpowers/
research/
articles/
coding_rules.txt